@pfarkya There are some existing tests in `test/parallel/test-url-….js` that you could take a look at, and we do have a small [guide](https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/master/doc/guides/writing-tests.md) on how to write tests – i hope that helps.

In order for people to review this, it would also be really helpful if you could expand a bit on what this PR does and why it does it in the commit message. You can use `git commit --amend` to edit the commit message and use `git push --force-with-lease` to update this PR afterwards.

All that being said, *if* we do change behaviour here, I would suggest aligning it more with the standardized `URL` parser, i.e. for an input of `http://unix/socketfile:/main` return an object with `unix` as the hostname and `/socketfile:/main` as the pathname, and no port.
